src/vendor/arrow/abi.h is the upstream file, byte for byte. It declares the
ArrowSchema and ArrowArray structs of the Arrow C Data Interface, a stable
ABI, and nothing else: no functions, no I/O, one #include <stdint.h>.
src/zu_arrow.c includes it; nothing else in the package does.

To update: set Version, Commit and the URLs to the new release tag, run

  curl -fsSL -o src/vendor/arrow/abi.h <File URL>
  curl -fsSL -o src/vendor/arrow/NOTICE.txt <Notice URL>

record the new SHA-256 lines (shasum -a 256), and run tools/verify-vendor.
The licence text only changes if Apache publishes a new one.

The SHA-256 values were computed at import time from the tag's raw files;
tools/verify-vendor downloads them again and fails on any difference, in
the vendored copies or upstream.
